  "notes": [
   "The award is the Cal-GETC pattern itself, so its area course lists are recorded as blocks; the page states no total units for the certificate, so total_units is null.",
   "The catalog prints codes zero-padded (e.g. BUS 060, MATH 020) while the closed list uses unpadded codes (BUS 60, MATH 20); these were treated as the same courses (catalog_addition false).",
   "Area 1 prints 'Select 3 courses, 9 units - One course from each area'; recorded as three sub-area blocks (1A, 1B, 1C) with the 9-unit area total noted here rather than on a block.",
   "Area 3 prints 'Minimum 6 units - 2 courses - One course from Arts and one course from Humanities'; recorded as 3A and 3B blocks each choosing one course.",
   "Area 4 requires 'Minimum 6 units - 2 courses from two academic disciplines'; the two-discipline constraint is not captured by the block rule.",
   "Area 5 prints '7-9 units, 2 courses required – one Physical Science and one Biological Science; at least one course from 5A or 5B must have a laboratory component (listed in 5C)'. 5C is recorded as a choose-one block but it is a lab constraint that largely overlaps 5A/5B, not necessarily an additional course; ASTRO 010L counts only with ASTRO 010 and ANTH 062L only with ANTH 062. ENVIR 010 may be certified in either 5A or 5B but only once.",
   "The U.S. History, Constitution, and American Ideals section is a CSU graduation requirement printed on this page, not a Cal-GETC area; its courses may also satisfy 6 units in Area 4. Option 2 consists of both the 'Option 2' block (POLS C1000) and the 'Option 2: PLUS one of the following' block; Option 1 is the alternative. Reviewer should check whether it belongs in this certificate's requirements.",
   "Area 6 requires the course be taken Fall 2021 or after.",
   "Courses listed in more than one area can only be used in one area.",
   "No program learning outcomes or careers are printed on this page."
  ]
